PaperlessLLM __VERSION__ for Windows (__ARCHITECTURE__)
====================================================

QUICK START - PORTABLE

1. Extract the complete ZIP archive to a normal folder.
2. Double-click PaperlessLLM.exe.
3. Your browser opens the local PaperlessLLM dashboard.

Keep PaperlessLLM.exe and paperless-llm.exe together. The first is the quiet,
double-clickable Windows launcher. The second runs the local background service
and also provides the command-line interface.

The executables include their C runtime and do not require a separate Microsoft
Visual C++ Redistributable installation.

OPTIONAL PER-USER INSTALLATION

Double-click "Install PaperlessLLM.cmd". It installs PaperlessLLM under your
Local AppData Programs directory, creates a Start menu shortcut, and asks
whether to create a Desktop shortcut. It does not require administrator rights.

You can later uninstall it through Windows Settings > Apps, or by running
"Uninstall PaperlessLLM.cmd" from the installed directory. Uninstalling removes
only application files and managed shortcuts. It deliberately preserves your
database, configuration, and logs. Saved credentials remain protected in
Windows Credential Manager.

SECURITY AND INTEGRITY

The installer verifies both executables against SHA256SUMS before copying them.
For download verification, compare the ZIP archive with the SHA-256 checksum
published alongside it on the GitHub release.

Do not place API keys or Paperless tokens in this release folder. Configure
them only inside the PaperlessLLM dashboard; PaperlessLLM stores them through
Windows Credential Manager. Do not publish or share your user data directory.

Windows may show a Microsoft Defender SmartScreen warning when an executable is
not yet signed by a widely trusted publisher. Verify that you downloaded the
release from the official GitHub repository and that its published SHA-256
checksum matches before choosing to run it.

COMMAND LINE

Open PowerShell in this directory and run:

  .\paperless-llm.exe --help

The default dashboard address is http://127.0.0.1:8765/ . PaperlessLLM binds to
localhost unless you explicitly configure LAN mode.

STOP / QUIT

Closing the browser does not stop the local PaperlessLLM service. In the
dashboard, choose "Quit PaperlessLLM" to shut it down cleanly. If the dashboard
is unavailable, end paperless-llm.exe in Task Manager; PaperlessLLM.exe is only
the short-lived launcher.

The docs directory includes native installation, security, release, and
backup/restore guidance.
